<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>Modeling with Differential Equations</title>

  <exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
      <p>Suppose a cylindrical tank with a hole in the
  bottom is filled with water.  Of course, the water will leak out and
  the height of the water in the tank will decrease.  Let's call the
  height <m>h(t)</m>.  Toricelli's Law says that
  <md>
  \frac{dh}{dt} = -k\sqrt{h}
  </md>
  where <m>k</m> is some constant.</p>
      <p>Suppose that the initial height of water in the
  tank is 100 cm and that, after five minutes, the height of water is
  81 cm.</p>
      <p>Find the height in the tank as a function of time and sketch a graph
  of <m>h(t)</m>.
  How long does it take for the water to drain out?</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that you continually put money into an account, which
  earns interest at an annual rate of 6% per year, at the rate of
  $5000 per year.  Let <m>B(t)</m> be the balance of the account.</p>
        <p>Write a differential equation that expresses the rate of change
  <m>dB/dt</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="3in">
      <statement>
        <p>Solve your differential equation for <m>B(t)</m> assuming that <m>B(0) =
  0</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>How long does it take to reach $50,000?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that you take out a mortgage of $100,000 at an interest
  rate of 4%.  Let <m>M(t)</m> be the amount that you owe on the mortgage
  after <m>t</m> years, which means that <m>M(0) = 100,000</m>.</p>
        <p>The interest you are paying causes the amount you owe to increase.
  Suppose that you are also paying <m>r</m> dollars per year on the mortgage.
  Set up a differential equation that describes <m>dM/dt</m>, the rate at
  which the amount you owe is changing.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="2in">
      <statement>
        <p>Solve the differential equation in terms of <m>r</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="2in">
      <statement>
        <p>If you want to pay off the mortgage after 30 years, what should the
  value of <m>r</m> be?  What is your monthly mortgage payment?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>How much will you have paid over the 30 years?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>What is the monthly mortgage payment if you want to pay off the
  mortgage after 20 years?  How much will you have paid over the 20
  years?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
